<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Log Today.

  On `android:configure`, which this file used to refuse. The refusal was
  half right: a settings screen between the tap that places a widget and the
  first tap that uses it IS a worse first run, and that is what the comment
  here defended. But the screen sets background strength and accent colour,
  which every card honours — this one already draws through
  `PrayerWidgetProvider.resolvedColors` — so leaving the attribute off did
  not remove a prompt, it removed the only way in. Placed widgets had no
  settings at all while the three prayer-times entries did, which is what a
  user reported.

  `configuration_optional` is the flag that wanted using: the launcher
  places the widget immediately and the screen becomes an entry in the
  long-press menu instead of a gate in front of it. `reconfigurable` is what
  puts that entry there. Both are API 31; below that Android falls back to
  prompting on placement, the same as the prayer widgets have always done.

  ONE ROW BY DEFAULT, not two. The card at one row is the same card with
  its header and its rule dropped and its chips shrunk — the five prayers,
  their times, and the countdown to the next, which is everything it is for.
  Two rows adds the date line back; three adds the practice graph. Every row
  buys something.

  maxResizeHeight is 600dp, not the 200dp it was. 200 stopped this widget
  at two launcher rows, which is where it was designed to live — but a card
  that cannot be dragged taller cannot show the practice graph, and the
  graph is the one thing people wanted from it that the prayer-times widget
  already had. Four rows is 432dp on a 420dpi phone; 600 covers the tallest
  cell a tablet is likely to report.

  updatePeriodMillis is 0 — this widget is pushed, never polled. It redraws
  when the payload changes, when a chip is tapped, and at each prayer
  boundary via ACTION_PRAYER_TIME_ELAPSED. A 30-minute poll would wake the
  device to redraw something that had not changed.
-->
<!--
  The API 31+ copy: identical to ../xml/prayer_widget_log_info.xml, but hidden from the picker.
  The Glance card of the same name is the entry now; this provider stays
  registered only so widgets a user placed before the switch keep drawing
  (docs/rewrite-plan.md, 4.3). Delete with the provider, once nobody has one placed.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:configure="com.prayer_times.PrayerWidgetConfigureActivity"
    android:widgetFeatures="reconfigurable|configuration_optional|hide_from_picker"
    android:description="@string/widget_description_log"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/prayer_widget_log"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="60dp"
    android:previewImage="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/prayer_widget_log_preview"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:minResizeWidth="250dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="60dp"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:maxResizeWidth="500dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="600dp" />
